The 0.87 rather than higher: there's a small residual uncertainty around whether "task completion" is defined narrowly (e.g. only successful HTTP 200s) versus broadly (e.g. quality-adjusted completion). But the 68% vs 22% gap combined with the nature of the fixes — latency and retries are load-bearing infrastructure for agentic workloads — makes this a clear choice.
